<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-11959] NullPointerException If transaction failed and failure handler doesn&apos;t configured explicitly</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-11959</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;In &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-9082&quot; title=&quot;Throwing checked exception during tx commit without node stopping leads to data corruption&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-9082&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-9082&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#160;was introduced code in IgniteTxAdapter:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
            U.error(log, &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;.format(fmt, commit, CU.txString(&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;),
                cctx.gridConfig().getFailureHandler().getClass().getSimpleName()), e);
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We get NullPointerException, If failureHander doesn&apos;t configured explicitly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Information about configured failureHandler is printed in FailureProcessor logic. I think we could remove failureHandler classname from such log messages.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
